      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Voltage, also referred to as Electric Tension, is the difference between electrical potentials of two points. For an electric field within a medium, (U_{ab} = - \\int_{r_a}^{r_b} E . {dr}), where (E) is electric field strength. For an irrotational electric field, the voltage is independent of the path between the two points (a) and (b)."
      }
    ],
